 "text": "This is going to matter once it gets cold outside, because guess who's looking for somewhere warm to live? Mice. And you won't even know until there are droppings in your pantry. So put these out now. Just drop one wherever they get in, the pantry, under the sink, the garage, even the car. It's peppermint and cinnamon oil, so it smells fresh to us, but mice don't like it. No toxic chemicals, so it's safe around kids and pets. And honestly, the best part, no traps to empty. There are twelve in a bag, and each one lasts up to three months. So grab two bags and do the whole house before the cold hits. It's in the orange cart.",
